% token_split — charge one shared run back to participants deterministically

# Module: token-split

Create a pure TypeScript module exporting `splitTokens(totalTokens, contributions, mode)`.
`contributions` contains `{userId: string, weight: number}` and mode is
`weighted | equal | initiator`.

MUST conserve every token exactly, return non-negative integers, combine repeated
users, handle an empty list, fall back to equal when all weights are zero, and
break fractional remainders by fraction descending then userId ascending.
`initiator` charges the first contribution's user and emits zero for all others.
Reject negative/non-integer totals, invalid weights, and unknown modes. Do not
mutate input or perform I/O. Tests must cover 100 split three ways as 34/33/33.
